<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE ussf-432 ascent</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 USSF-432 (SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Loft: FALCON 9 FAMILY SURROGATE, not this flight: altitude &amp; downrange vs time from SpaceX webcast telemetry of Iridium NEXT-7
(F9 Block 5, VSFB SLC-4E, 25 Jul 2018, MECO T+146 s = USSF-432&#x27;s published MECO T+2:26), 9 s running mean; range = integral of horizontal speed x R/(R+h).
Telemetry source: https://github.com/shahar603/Telemetry-Data/tree/master/Iridium%20NEXT%207 (analysed.json). FILE ENDS AT T+508 s (telemetry end): USSF-432 SECO, orbit and deploy are NOT published (NSSL/NRO-class mission).
Events (SpaceX ussf432 timeline https://www.spacex.com/launches/ussf432): Max-Q 1:07, MECO 2:26, sep 2:29, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:55; booster entry 6:06-6:30, landing 8:26.
Azimuth basis: FAA/ZLA CARF NOTAM 10/377 (Area A) far-edge midpoint 32.733N -119.492E from LL2 pad = 153.56 deg; ZLA 10/378 Area B (154.0 deg) and
MMFR B3553 stage-1 area (~155.2 deg) consistent. Valid 2611030142-0604Z covers T0. Implies a ~70 deg-class plane (LL2 notes drop zones match Starlink Group 15; ASSUMED, unconfirmed).
T0: SpaceX + LL2 2026-11-03T01:42:00Z (Mon 2 Nov 5:42 pm PST, window opens; 4 h window), booster 8th flight (LL2: B1095 -&gt; OCISLY).
Velocity = d/dt of interpolated altitude and ground range (Earth-relative). Payload mass/orbit unpublished: loft is the family profile only.
Pad (LL2): 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=153.56 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-03T01:42:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
